+# Motion Trimmer → Video · offline review build
+
+Base: `378d6f4`. Spec pinned: `shuenrui/singular-flows@960213c`, Motion Trimmer Video v0.0.2 overrides v0.0.1. This README describes implementation, not a live quality or billing result.
+
+## Status and safety gates
+- Built and tested locally with explicitly fake inference replies and a synthetic, locally generated 1-second MP4. No paid inference, authentication discovery, deployment or external push was performed.
+- **Real video generation is disabled.** `js/video.js` has a single `FIELDS` map: duration, aspectRatio and audio are all `null`. The ordinary request builder omits all three; the runtime refuses POST while duration is unconfirmed. Do not enable this based on a price-table field name.
+- June must document/confirm gateway duration forwarding. Aspect ratio and audio remain unspecified; there are no controls or portrait/audio promises. Then obtain separate user approval and a capped key for acceptance #12: one 5-second 480p Wan adapter-validation render (a controlled diagnostic, not the normal 720p UI), confirm media duration/resolution, content download and settled charge. That live check has NOT been performed. Do not claim live end-to-end completion.
+- Offline tests inject `fixture_duration` via the same map to exercise the complete UI. It is deliberately not a production field name and is never configured by the gallery. There is no URL/query/localStorage release override.
+
+## Use
+Run `python3 proxy.py 8730` from this extracted folder; open `http://localhost:8730/#/skills`. This is a local review command, not deployment authorization. Existing Settings owns the API key. Planning is a paid text operation only when the user explicitly clicks Plan; reviewing prices is public. The old Motion Trimmer remains planning-only and its existing request is unchanged.
+
+The new card opens one modal: brief/context/platform → 5/10/15-second plan → editable JSON shot beats/overlays/dropped details and separate editable prompt → Refresh exact price → explicit Generate approval → queued/processing → inline Blob player/Download MP4. There is no automatic video fallback, regeneration, composition, stitching, music or uploaded assets. Overlays are editor instructions, not burned into the MP4. Exact typography, brand assets, easing and second-perfect edits are not promised. Review generated prompts before any future approved render.
+
+Video choices are only `alibaba/wan-3.0/text-to-video` at 720p (default, 15 seconds) and `minimax/h3-max-turbo` at 768p. Exact public-config prices are refreshed for review and checked again before POST. Unknown config/pricing blocks. Planner uses one structured `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5` call, with `deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017` only after a 5xx; invalid JSON and auth/credit/rate/network failures do not trigger a fallback. Each attempt has a $0.10 heuristic preflight, not a billing cap. Planner estimated usage receipts and video quoted/pending/settled receipts are separate; missing cost never means zero.
+
+## Recovery and privacy
+Only minimal job references, quoted configuration/cost, opaque idempotency token, request hash and creating-key hash are retained in `motion-video.v1`. No prompt, API key, Authorization header or result URL is persisted there. The opaque idempotency token is not the API credential. Up to 20 references are retained; full/unreadable recovery storage fails closed. Do not clear browser recovery data while a creation may be outstanding.
+
+Double clicks are locked before awaits. A lost create response is uncertain, not free or cancelled. Retry is explicit and uses the same token and byte-identical body. After reload, re-enter the identical prompt/configuration to retry an uncertain creation; an edited body is refused, not sent under a fresh token. A known job resumes with GET only and the creating key. No automatic POST is made on reload. Auth/credit/not-found/network failures remain distinct from failed generation and failed content download. A definite create-time 401/402 is a rejected submission with no created job; it can be replaced explicitly after fixing Settings/credits. Network/5xx/ambiguous responses remain uncertain and must not be treated as uncharged. A completed job whose download fails is still charged; Retry download only never generates another job. Terminal versions stay in the job-reference selector for later authenticated re-download.
+
+Polling uses bounded backoff and a 3-minute local deadline, with bounded requests. Explicit Resume starts a new local observation interval. Closing/pagehide stops polling, not the upstream job; no cancellation/refund promise. Changing the key requires closing/reopening the flow; a key hash prevents accidentally resuming with a different key. Recovery depends on retaining the exact creating key in existing Settings. JSON edits are validated for numeric duration totals and typed in-range overlays; this does not prove creative truth or semantic model compliance.
+
+Content always uses `/v1/videos/{validated-id}/content`, authenticated fetch, and a memory-only Blob URL. Absolute gateway content URLs may validate to that exact path, but arbitrary hosts, paths, queries, fragments and redirects are rejected and never followed. Keys are never inserted into media URLs. Blob URLs are revoked on replacement/close. The proxy forwards Idempotency-Key only on POST `/v1/videos`, streams bounded chunks with a 100 MiB maximum, and does not follow media redirects. Known oversized content returns 413; unknown oversize streams are cut off within the limit (matching the documented bounded-transfer behavior).
+
+## Review and operational handoff
+No live server has been replaced. Before any later authorized deployment, back up the current runtime and exact start configuration. Extract into a new reviewed directory, compare the supplied SHA256, run the local smoke/security checks, then restart the exact owning proxy process using the owner's existing process manager. Do not launch a second listener on an occupied port. Verify root 200, legacy flows and GET/HEAD source-denial 404 after restart; rollback by restoring the prior runtime and restarting that exact service. A public source branch or ZIP is not a deployment.
+
+The ZIP contains runtime files and this README only: no private design, test Python, reports, API credentials, pricing snapshots, caches or build artifacts. `proxy.py` is required runtime Python, not private test source. Local evidence and tests stay outside the runtime ZIP. `reports/motion-video/EVIDENCE.md` in the source worktree indexes all 12 criteria, honest blocked live verification, red/green logs, regression bodies, source hashes, package CRC/byte checks and copied-package tests. Independent parent review remains required before publication.
